;; Stone 255.12 NON-VACUITY, macro registry — why `ast_same_identity`'s
;; `is_reference()` requirement must NOT be relaxed.
;;
;; The two templates differ only in `v` (a LET BINDER symbol) vs `:v` (a keyword).
;; A binder is not a reference, so the cross-spelling arm refuses to equate them
;; and these stay two macros. Relaxing `is_reference()` — the cure the 255.12
;; brief proposed for site 2 — would make this file freeze CLEAN and silently
;; discard the second template.
(:wat::core::defmacro :p255_12::MB [x <- :wat::WatAST] -> :wat::WatAST
  `(:wat::core::let [v ~x] v))
(:wat::core::defmacro :p255_12::MB [x <- :wat::WatAST] -> :wat::WatAST
  `(:wat::core::let [v ~x] :v))
